    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0804" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg716"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-04-01"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 92.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a note from the Japanese
                    minister at this capital indicating the course which, he states, the Russian
                    Government has agreed to follow in the matter of communicating information to
                    you concerning such Japanese prisoners of war as may fall into their hands.</p>
                <p>You will bring the matter to the attention of the Russian foreign office, and ask
                    that the regular communication agreed upon may be made to you without your
                    making request therefor in each case.</p>
                <p>You will communicate the information received to the Japanese minister at
                    Berlin.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d690-a1.xml" xpointer="d690-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
